{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":1502105,"title":"why is entropy portrayed as evil in the world of darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-04T08:33:34-08:00","id":1502105,"title":"why is entropy portrayed as evil in the world of darkness","content":"most things having to do with entropy and death in the wod are portrayed as evil. why is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T09:26:16-08:00","id":1502107,"title":"","content":"Because the WoD is meant to be a horror game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T10:12:20-08:00","id":1502111,"title":"","content":"Because the fundamental goal of life is to make more life and avoid death and things that kill you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T11:16:03-08:00","id":1502115,"title":"","content":"Well it is ultimatly the soarce of much of our woes irl. Everything is constantly pushing against it but it seems likely to drag everything down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T11:17:32-08:00","id":1502116,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting point. In fact, I seem to recall that one of the last books during the WoD's initial run back in the early 00s flat out said that the Sphere of Entropy had been corrupted somewhere along the line. I <i>think</i> it might have been in the Revised Euthanatos Tradition Book, though maybe it's was in Ascension. It involved an Archmaster of Entropy attempting to fix the Sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:20:58-08:00","id":1502145,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that while Entropy frequently gets associated with or portrayed as evil in the WoD, it's important to note that it's not the only source of ill in the world. From the perspective of the Traditions, the Technocracy-as-Stasis is arguably a bigger problem from day to day. And many Garou oppose the Weaver just as much as the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Other gamelines don't directly associate Entropy with evil, but they do often come with some notion that there is something wrong with the world, or that it is heading into a low point in the cosmic cycle. And the forces of Entropy in the world are some of the best suited for manifesting that corruption, especially when your game embraces horror themes and aesthetics, as mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:42:33-08:00","id":1502148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502116#post1502116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting point. In fact, I seem to recall that one of the last books during the WoD's initial run back in the early 00s flat out said that the Sphere of Entropy had been corrupted somewhere along the line. I <i>think</i> it might have been in the Revised Euthanatos Tradition Book, though maybe it's was in Ascension. It involved an Archmaster of Entropy attempting to fix the Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>you mean, it wasn't always like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:46:46-08:00","id":1502150,"title":"","content":"Apparently not; although we have no idea how long it's been since it was corrupted. It <i>may</i> be connected to the Wyrm; or not. It's certainly been like that for a <i>long </i>time. But yeah; it's entirely possible that it wasn't <i>always </i>like that. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:50:06-08:00","id":1502151,"title":"","content":"Because the metaphysical embodiment of Entropy has gone insane in a way that is much more tangible that the one of Stasis (who was a subtler penchant for halting progress) or the one for Dynamism (who is chaotic by nature and supposed to be insane). The Underworld being consumed by its embodiment, Pentex actively poisoning the world via its actions, Jhor driving mages to new levels of fatalistic madness, the nearly inevitable erosion of the self caused by vampirism, the Wheel of Ages being at a point where karmic fates more easily lead to ruin, imagination and possibility leaving the world, and many more.<br /> <br /> Death makes you lose your Avatar, so all the endless horizons you could explore are now gone, replaced by the much more limited powers of a ghost. You are like a painter gone blind, a composer gone deaf, you can remember where the power was, but the power you can touch is only a memory. You may attempt to reach out with all your world changing passion, but in the end, you cannot touch the shadow strangling hearts and minds, hope and potentials. Now the furnace of passion in your own heart can only burn you in your own flame.<br /> <br /> The end results of Entropy are terrifying to a mage on many levels, even though those more well informed know its not working as intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:54:03-08:00","id":1502153,"title":"","content":"Reminds me of the Shin Megami Tensai Games. Basically most people are so used that Order means Peaceful, Stable and -and this is the pointe- free Life.<br /> Everything that disrupts this quit peace full days is seen as destroyer peace and so evil. But Order itself is only meaning Peace and Stability.<br /> Freedom itself is an aspect of Chaos. So people actually most of the time would have to choose between peace and stability or strife and freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T05:28:24-08:00","id":1502197,"title":"","content":"Evil basically boils down to what humans deem harmful to us. We fear pain of both physical and emotional origin, we fear death and the lack of understanding of what follows.<br /> We don't like it when the things that make us happy stop making us happy or start upsetting us. Be that because we lost that thing through destruction or death, because our personality has changed, we fall out of love or whatever.<br /> <br /> Point being; death and change typically scare us and make us experience other negative emotions, and so they are bad. Fictional personifications of those things that bring us misery are thus evil.<br /> (On an objective level, WoD's Entropy is antagonistic because it's out of balance due to Stasis overwhelming it due to that hatred/fear of change and endings.)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 02-05-2023, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:15:05-08:00","id":1502263,"title":"","content":"The idea of a metaphisical Triad comes directly from hinduism - the WoD one, not the Christian kind.<br /> <br /> In Hinduism, you have Brahma the Creator, Vishnu the Keeper and Shiva the Destroyer. In some traditions hinduism is even monotheistic-like, with the 3 being aspects of the same one being, and every other Gods being aspects of them - sorta like Avatars of those.<br /> <br /> &quot;Avatar&quot; by the way also comes from hinduism - it's a demi-god encarnation of a God, like Krishna for instance, who is the 9th Avatar of Brahma, and probably the most well know of all hinduist Avatars, with Krishna being one of the most beloved of all mythic figures in hinduism.<br /> <br /> Some gurus even compare Krishna with Christ (to the horror of Christians), and in a sense, Jesus could be called as an &quot;Avatar&quot; of the God of Israel - what Jesus is for Christians is exactly what avatars in hinduism are.<br /> <br /> Anyway, despite the literally MILLIONS of Gods in hinduism - and the reason that they have so many is that there are minor Gods for everything, including Gods for individual families, somewhat akin to the idea of personal &quot;guardian angels&quot; for christians (mostly for catholics thou), however, the most worshipped God of all in hinduism is Shiva, the Destroyer.<br /> <br /> Shiva is the yoga dancer, a serene God and basically the one that invented meditation. Hmmm... A God of Destruction... That meditates? Seems... Off. Right?<br /> <br /> Well, Shiva is considered the ultimate benevolence. Shiva is supposed to &quot;turn the lights off&quot; at the very end of the Universe, &quot;undoing&quot; even all the other Gods at the end of the cicle.<br /> <br /> AKA, Shiva is the one who will be responsible to destroy EVERYTHING by the end of the cicle.<br /> <br /> Remember all the Nefandi and Spectres and Wyrm that wish to destroy the Tellurian? Well, that's Shiva's job.<br /> <br /> His wife is Kali, who is the Goddess of DEATH (quite appropriate for &quot;The Destroyer&quot;), and Kali on her own end, is an aspect of Parvati who, surprise surprise, is the Goddess of LIFE.<br /> <br /> (In fact, in some traditions, Kali and Parvati are the two coins of the same entity... Hindu Gods are weird for us to understand and it's hard to explain, their theological concepts are completely different from our christian cultural base)<br /> <br /> Shiva is venerated even by DEMONS (Rakshasa or something like it, Im not sure I spelled it right, cut me some slack) - but not because he is evil, quite the contrary, it's because Shiva is the ultimate good and ultimate justice. There are even stances upon which Shiva judged on the side of the demons against the Gods, when those were in the right. ALL are equal for lord Shiva.<br /> <br /> And his wife Kali is an exceptional demon hunter by the way.<br /> <br /> You see, I think that this idea that Entropy is bad comes from a western view of eastern ideas. The Triad is unquestionably hinduist in origin.<br /> <br /> But, death and destruction is undeniably viewed as &quot;evil&quot; in western culture. When you die, you go to paradise, were everything is ETERNAL. Death is a punishment due to the original sin, and we live in a world of death and decay because of it.<br /> <br /> Even an atheist like myself have that christian cultural heritage. <br /> <br /> But in hinduism, life, creation, death and destruction are weaves of the same fabric, and are all part of an endless cicle of reencarnation.<br /> <br /> Therefore, my take is that the reason why Entropy is considered bad is simply that it was an eastern idea that was misunderstood under a western viewpoint","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:25:19-08:00","id":1502264,"title":"","content":"One final note: Shiva the Destroyer, is supposed to destroy the entire universe by the end of the cicle... So that a new universe can be born, and a new cicle begins.<br /> <br /> The old must give way for the new to be created.<br /> <br /> What I find interesting is that the writers managed to get this part right... But then proceeded to say that this is bad... What?<br /> <br /> I can only conclude that the original writers drunk on hinduism for inspiration and got the right idea, but following writers that saw that gave it a look and said &quot;oh my God, burn it with Holy Fire! You shall feel my divine wrath, fiend!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's the only explanation.<br /> <br /> PS: I would actually find it MASSIVELY entertaining to have Chorists, Hermetics and other western traditions having endles theological bickering with eastern traditions over the evil/good nature of destruction, and having the western traditions outright denying &quot;Entropy&quot; as a &quot;fundamental force&quot; (not the Sphere), and saying that it is an &quot;evil anathema that must be purged&quot;, while the easterns claim it to be an &quot;integral part of the natural cicle&quot;, and watching they kill each other over it while I eat popcorn, I think this would be absolutely majestic to have in the game but, oh well, &quot;Entropy is evil&quot;, what can I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:50:51-08:00","id":1502265,"title":"","content":"The real reason? Because 1st ed Mage drew a lot of its cosmology, especially regarding things like Entropy and The Marauders from 1st ed Werewolf's Triat. 2nd ed moved away from that, establishing its own separate-but-similar metaphysics, but a lot of artifacts, especially the idea of the Euthanatoi and their signature sphere being &quot;tainted&quot;, continued to pop up.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:50:08-08:00","id":1502274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502265#post1502265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real reason? Because 1st ed Mage drew a lot of its cosmology, especially regarding things like Entropy and The Marauders from 1st ed Werewolf's Triat. 2nd ed moved away from that, establishing its own separate-but-similar metaphysics, but a lot of artifacts, especially the idea of the Euthanatoi and their signature sphere being &quot;tainted&quot;, continued to pop up.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for explaining in a much more pragmatic and concise manner than I ever would be capable of haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T01:36:45-08:00","id":1502291,"title":"","content":"BTW, this is also a large part of why the 1st ed Ahl i Batin don't use Entropy, as they are kind of presented as the without-flaw &quot;too perfect for this world&quot; masterminds secretly responsible for all of the setting's history, from the creation of the Council of Nine to where the new hotness that is the Digital Web &quot;really&quot; comes from. As such unicorns, they have to be free of &quot;Wyrm taint&quot;. <br /> <br /> (And again, this is one of those 1st ed artifacts that would keep cropping up even though later material moved away from it, with Mage: The Sorcerers Crusade mostly ignoring it and having them use Entropy like everyone else and their initial revised edition write up having it only be a small faction of extremists who refused to use the sphere.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T09:01:09-08:00","id":1502308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502291#post1502291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, this is also a large part of why the 1st ed Ahl i Batin don't use Entropy, as they are kind of presented as the without-flaw &quot;too perfect for this world&quot; masterminds secretly responsible for all of the setting's history, from the creation of the Council of Nine to where the new hotness that is the Digital Web &quot;really&quot; comes from. As such unicorns, they have to be free of &quot;Wyrm taint&quot;.<br /> <br /> (And again, this is one of those 1st ed artifacts that would keep cropping up even though later material moved away from it, with Mage: The Sorcerers Crusade mostly ignoring it and having them use Entropy like everyone else and their initial revised edition write up having it only be a small faction of extremists who refused to use the sphere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ive always hated that absolute nonsense about the Batini not using &quot;Entropy&quot;... I was like &quot;what the hell? They dont use FATE Magic? The master manipulators? Get the hell out of here&quot;.<br /> <br /> I just simply ignored it completely from the very first time I played that game as if it wasnt even there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T15:51:15-08:00","id":1502328,"title":"","content":"Honestly (IMO at least) Entropy really should be Fate, as it feels more appropriate for both the Traditions as a whole and most of the Traditions (and crafts) individually. This is especially true in the Sorcerers Crusade setting, where they were willing to rename Correspondence to the more period (and Batini) suitable Connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-06-2023, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:33:23-08:00","id":1502422,"title":"","content":"About a decade ago, shortly after M20 first came out, I started a thread about giving Sphere variants to each of the Traditions, reflecting each one's unique insights into one or two Spheres. When it came to the Euthanatoi, the conclusion that I reached is that Entropy, as written, ought to <i>be </i>their Sphere variant; and everyone <i>else </i>should be using a Fate Sphere. It isn't that the Euthanatoi don't use Fate magick; they absolutely <i>do</i>. Rather, they see Fate as something cyclical and tied to the cycle of life, death, and rebirth. The other Traditions are so bothered by the \u201cdeath\u201d part of that (as mentioned near the beginning of this thread) that they downplay or outright ignore that aspect of the Sphere, leaning more into the \u201cdestiny, fate, and fortune\u201d angle while ignoring the \u201cdoom\u201d aspects.<br /> <br /> The Verbenae are the only other Tradition that comes close to the Euthanatoi in this regard, with their veneration of the cycle of the seasons; but they view it primarily in terms of Life. The Euthanatoi have a reputation for being death-oriented because they're the only ones who acknowledge the role that death plays in the cycle; one could argue that they're the only ones who view the Wheel of Fate in a balanced manner. \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T14:05:16-08:00","id":1502434,"title":"","content":"It still seems odd that they would poach from thermodynamics instead of using any other word from mystic cultural backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T15:28:50-08:00","id":1502452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502434#post1502434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still seems odd that they would poach from thermodynamics instead of using any other word from mystic cultural backgrounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the reason is the inverse to why you first understand &quot;Spirit&quot; to only then understand &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;. If someone told you about &quot;Anthropic Fields&quot; before you know that this translates to &quot;Spirit&quot;, you'd be &quot;wtf is this nerd talking about&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, just saying &quot;Fate 1 senses destiny, Fate 2 manipulates simple destiny, Fate 3 allows you to erode matter or make a broken machine start working&quot; you would be wondering what relation those things have with each other and you would only conclude that the &quot;Fate&quot; Sphere is just a collection of loose powers with no connection between each other.<br /> <br /> That's why I believe they went with the &quot;Thermodynamics&quot; angle, for better understanding of what it encompass","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T17:47:53-08:00","id":1502469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502434#post1502434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still seems odd that they would poach from thermodynamics instead of using any other word from mystic cultural backgrounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that there's no good name for the whole Sphere. [Entropy], for lack of anything better to call it, actually spans the full Metaphysical Trinity in much the same way that Prime does; but where Prime is the ultimate source of everything, [Entropy] is the ultimate sink. In its Dynamic aspect, [Entropy] is about luck and fortune; in its Static aspect, [Entropy] is about predestined outcomes; and in its Entropic aspect, [Entropy] is about decay, destruction, and death. But finding a single word that encompasses luck/fortune, destiny/fate, and decay/death is <i>hard. </i>I have tried to find a good one over the years, and have thus far come up empty.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could call it Endings? That's a bit of a stretch for the luck/fortune side of it (though not too much of one); but it fits both destiny/fate and decay/death quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-08-2023, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T06:26:11-08:00","id":1502506,"title":"","content":"I feel like Destiny itself could fit because even being Lucky or not is something that is detirmed at birth. Fated Encounters are self explaining in this and so even death is one big that you can not escape. But yeah Entropy feels itself better once the other person understood the basics because the difference between Luck and Fated Encounters is a whole theory for itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T09:03:17-08:00","id":1502519,"title":"","content":"It depends on your Paradigm, actually: of you view the world as one where there's a divine order, then the notion of fate and destiny will be front and center when you consider [Entropy], and \u201cbeing lucky is something determined at birth\u201d. But if your view of reality is that everything is chaos, then you're more likely to view [Entropy] as the Sphere of luck and chance; Destiny <i>does not fit</i> with such a worldview. And if you have a nihilistic view of reality (like the Hollow Ones), you'll tend to view [Entropy] as the Sphere of death and decay. Again, Destiny doesn't fit for this, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T10:43:04-08:00","id":1502521,"title":"","content":"In fairness, we don't really hold any of the other Sphere names to this standard. At the time the Traditions formed, for instance, Matter did not mean physical material and it wouldn't for a fair few centuries. Prime is another one that should be quite worldview specific and only has cohesion because it relates to a game mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T11:44:38-08:00","id":1502529,"title":"","content":"For me, the issue isn't that \u201cEntropy\u201d is a scientific word; it's that it's so specifically related to the \u201cthings fall apart\u201d concept, when there's so much more to the Sphere than that. It would be like naming Forces \u201cFire\u201d, or Matter \u201cEarth\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T12:38:34-08:00","id":1502532,"title":"","content":"Well the Sphere is trying to be too many things at once, its always going to have a naming problem. The concepts of the Sphere aren't actually aligned, they just happen to be different definitions of the same word. <br /> <br /> The best name is probably Fortune, though that still relies heavily on multiple contradictory definitions of the word, and it requires a bit of makeshift poetry (death and decay are the fate of all things or something like that). It's the same messy equivocation dance as Entropy, it just conveys the other possibilities slightly better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T13:00:16-08:00","id":1502534,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the real reason is that Stewart Wieck was probably a math geek. This would also explain the use of Correspondence rather than Connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:06:22-08:00","id":1503382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502328#post1502328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly (IMO at least) Entropy really should be Fate, as it feels more appropriate for both the Traditions as a whole and most of the Traditions (and crafts) individually. This is especially true in the Sorcerers Crusade setting, where they were willing to rename Correspondence to the more period (and Batini) suitable Connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of Magick being called Entropy (rather than Order and Chaos, Destiny, or Fate) - and possibly being rather unique and particular in it's variety and wide range of possible effects, results, motifs, and also themes - could come to a considerable and significant extent from the outlining, design, and development of MtA's 1st edition (maybe the Corebook in particular).The tone and the mood were distinctly both otherworldy, supernatural, and definitely gothic-punk. The reach and influence of Technocrats on all various matters, topics, and areas was also mentioned, shown, and detailed quite extensively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T08:40:23-07:00","id":1509725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1502105-why-is-entropy-portrayed-as-evil-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=1502264#post1502264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One final note: Shiva the Destroyer, is supposed to destroy the entire universe by the end of the cicle... So that a new universe can be born, and a new cicle begins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that this is why, in WoD, entropy is broken. Entropy is supposed to recycle, but the recycling process is broken, so it just destroys. In WoD, the concept of the heat death of the universe is a manifestation of that. The Universe will not re-emerge. It will <b>end, it will freeze</b>. It <u>should</u> re-emerge but entropy is broken due to the fuckery of A) the Wyrm, B) the Nephandi (who want to to remain ended) and C) Voormas, who poisoned the sphere itself due to his paralysing fear of death, to finally becoming that.<br /> <br /> Effectively, the reason entropy is associated with something bad, is because it doesn't work as it should. A mage can actually use the correct type of entropy (due to them saying fuck you to reality through their avatars), but it's resonance is somewhat tainted and it can take them down if they aren't careful - because Voormas has poisoned the idea itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}